burundi-law: licence and the terms of each source

1. Lexifina's own work: CC0 1.0

The arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the folder layout, the tables, README files and tools are
Lexifina's own work and are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

2. Law text: Bulletin Officiel du Burundi, from amategeko.gov.bi

The text of the Constitution, codes, lois, décrets-lois, décrets, ordonnances and other acts in constitution/, codes/,
lois/, decrets-lois/, decrets/, ordonnances/, arretes/ and autres-actes/ is copied from the PDFs of the Bulletin
Officiel du Burundi published on "Mémoire du Droit Burundais", the legal portal of the Ministry of Justice of the
Republic of Burundi (https://amategeko.gov.bi; "une propriété du Ministère ayant la justice dans ses attributions"),
retrieved from 26 November 2026. The portal states no terms of use. These are official texts of the Republic of
Burundi, published so that the public may know the law; Burundi's copyright act (Loi n°1/021 du 30 décembre 2005
portant protection du droit d'auteur et des droits voisins au Burundi) excludes official texts of a legislative,
administrative or judicial nature from protection. Only the published text is copied. Changes made by Lexifina: the
text of each act is split into one file per article, the line breaks of the printed columns are joined, and running
page headers and the "Divers" part of each issue (notices to private persons) are left out. Nothing is translated or
corrected.

3. Metadata from earlier builds

catalogue/, treaties/: metadata (titles, dates, numbers, links) from WIPO Lex, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/,
retrieved 30 October 2026. Source: World Intellectual Property Organization. WIPO content is published under CC BY 4.0
(https://www.wipo.int/web/terms-of-use); only facts are copied. WIPO does not endorse this repository.
Catalogue entries for the laws of 2003-2012: facts from the file names in the public media index of the Assemblée
nationale du Burundi, https://assemblee.bi/, retrieved 30 October 2026.
un-treaties/: treaty actions from the UN Treaty Collection, https://treaties.un.org/, facts only.
legal-system/: open facts from Wikidata, https://www.wikidata.org/ (CC0 1.0).
